{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And this shall be your southern border.</b> A southern direction — from east to west." "<b>From the wilderness of Zin.</b> Which is beside Edom — it begins from the southeast corner of the land of the nine tribes. How so? Three lands sit along the south of the land of Israel, one beside the other — part of the land of Egypt, and the whole land of Edom, and the whole land of Moab. The land of Egypt is at the southwest corner, as it says in this pericah: ״from Azmon to the brook of Egypt, and its termini are the sea,״ and the brook of Egypt ran along the face of the whole land of Egypt, as it says (Joshua 13): ״from the Shihor which is before Egypt,״ and it separates between the land of Egypt and the land of Israel. And the land of Edom is beside it toward the east, and the land of Moab beside the land of Edom at the end of the south toward the east. And when Israel came out of Egypt, if the Omnipresent had wanted to hasten their entry into the land, He would have taken them across the Nile toward the north and they would have entered the land of Israel — but He did not do so. And this is what is said (Exodus 13): ״And Elohim did not lead them by the way of the land of the Philistines״ — for they dwell by the sea on the west of the land of Canaan, as is said of the Philistines (Zephaniah 2): ״O inhabitants of the coast of the sea, O nation of the Cherethites.״ And He did not lead them by that way, but turned them and brought them out by way of the south into the wilderness — and this is what Ezekiel (Ezekiel 20) called ״the wilderness of the peoples,״ because many nations dwelt alongside it. And they traveled along its south from west toward east always until they came to the south of the land of Edom, and they asked the king of Edom to let them pass through his land and enter the land along its breadth — but he refused, and they were forced to go around the entire south of Edom until they came to the south of the land of Moab, as it says (Judges 11): ״and also to the king of Moab he sent, and he refused.״ And they walked along the entire south of Moab to its end, and from there they turned their faces northward until they had circled the entire eastern flank to its breadth; and when they finished its east, they found the land of Sihon and Og, who dwelt east of the land of Canaan, with the Jordan separating between them. And this is what is said of Jephthah (ibid.): ״and he went through the wilderness and circled the land of Edom and the land of Moab, and came from the east of the sun to the land of Moab.״ And they conquered the land of Sihon and Og, which was north of the land of Moab, and came close to the Jordan — and this is opposite the northwest corner of the land of Moab. It is thus found that the land of Canaan, which is across the Jordan to the west, had its southeast corner beside Edom."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:48.509333999Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}